"The project is complete and verified. Here's a summary:\n\n## What was created\n\n**`fmtcsv.py`** — the CLI tool:\n- `summarize_csv(path)` → returns `(row_count, column_count, first_data_row)` using Python's `csv` module, so quoted fields with embedded commas parse correctly and field content (including spaces inside quotes) is preserved exactly.\n- Counts exclude the header row; empty/header-only files are handled gracefully.\n- `main()` provides the `fmtcsv <file>` CLI via `argparse`, printing:\n  ```\n  Total rows: N\n  Total columns: N\n  First data row: [...]\n  ```\n\n**`test_fmtcsv.py`** — 8 pytest tests covering:\n- basic row/column counts\n- quoted field containing a comma (and escaped quotes)\n- leading/trailing spaces preserved inside quotes\n- combined comma + spaces in quotes\n- empty file and header-only file\n- CLI end-to-end via `main([path])` with `capsys`\n- `format_summary` output for the empty case\n\n## Test results\n\n```\n8 passed in 0.01s\n```\n\nAll 8 tests pass. \n\n## Demo\n\n```console\n$ printf 'name,age,note\\n\"Doe, Jane\",30,\"  keeps spaces  \"\\nBob,25,plain\\n' > /tmp/demo.csv\n$ .venv/bin/python fmtcsv.py /tmp/demo.csv\nTotal rows: 2\nTotal columns: 3\nFirst data row: ['Doe, Jane', '30', '  keeps spaces  ']\n```\n\nNote: the system Python venv was read-only, so I created a local `.venv` in the workspace with pytest installed. Run tests with `.venv/bin/python -m pytest test_fmtcsv.py -v`."